{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Fix ready for review — pushing to Gerrit\n\nFollowed /rebar-debug. The pre-existing RCA on this ticket was confirmed exactly against the current tree (line numbers shifted, structure identical). Implemented the ticket's own fix plan.\n\n### Root cause (confirmed)\n`provision_store` in `infra/scripts/mcp-entrypoint.sh` serialized the tickets clear+clone (fd 9, on the tracker inode) and the code clone (fd 8, on the code-dir inode), released both locks, then ran the ensure step — `sh \"${MCP_ENSURE_SCRIPT}\" \"${REBAR_TRACKER_DIR}\"` — **UNLOCKED**. That ensure step (`reviewbot-ensure-tickets.sh` → `rebar._store.ensures.run_ensures`) takes rebar's write lock by creating `.ticket-write.lock` / `.ticket-write.lock.d` **inside** the store. So a launch path mutates the shared tracker volume outside the serialization the same file's clear+clone steps rely on. Consequences: a single stray entry makes a concurrent container's `git clone` fail (\"destination path already exists and is not an empty directory\"); the peer's `clear_dir` (`rm -rf ./.[!.]*`) then unlinks a live rebar lock, breaking mutual exclusion in both directions. This violated the file's own contract comment (\"serialization has to live HERE\").\n\n### Enumerated launch paths (AC1)\nThe provisioning writers to the shared tracker volume are: (1) tickets re-clone (`reclone_store`), (2) code checkout (`clone_code`), (3) the ensure step. (1) and (2) were serialized; (3) was the bypass. Documented all three plus the invariant in the expanded serialization header.\n\n### Fix\n- Factored a single reusable `with_dir_lock <dir> <label> <cmd>` seam (AC3). Uses one fixed fd 9 (the three calls are strictly sequential and never nested, so no fd aliasing) — this deliberately avoids `eval`/parameterized-fd and stays shellcheck-clean. `set -e` safe (`\"$@\" || wdl_rc=$?`).\n- Routed all three shared-volume writers through it: `reclone_store` → `reclone_store_locked`, `clone_code` → `clone_code_locked`, and the ensure step via new `ensure_store` under `with_dir_lock` on the tracker inode (for safe absolute tracker dirs; unsafe/relative dirs run unlocked, preserving the soft-failure posture that the existing unsafe-dir tests assert).\n- Recorded the AC2 decision in the header: compose `mcp:` service keeps `restart: always` on 8091 (no topology change).\n\n### Proof it has teeth\n- New RED test `test_the_ensure_step_does_not_run_while_a_peer_holds_the_store_lock` FAILS on the unmodified script for the right reason (ensure ran while a peer held the store lock), PASSES with the fix. Mutation check: re-introducing the defect returns it to RED.\n- Coverage pin `test_the_code_checkout_is_not_cloned_while_a_peer_holds_its_lock`.\n- Full dedicated suite `test_mcp_entrypoint_provisioning.py`: 21 pass (was 19).\n\n### Verification\n- `make lint` (shellcheck) PASS · `make typecheck` PASS.\n- Targeted infra/entrypoint/ensure/store suites: 135 pass (49 scripts incl. autodeploy bluegreen / reviewbot entrypoint / mcp client PATs; 86 unit incl. entrypoint provisioning, reviewbot ensure, on-box infra, autodeploy prune). Change is isolated to one shell script + its dedicated test — nothing else imports/execs it. Gerrit `Verified` runs the authoritative full suite.\n\n### Scope check\nMechanical \"route the bypassing launch path through the existing lock\" — no deploy design/topology change, so landing per instructions (not escalating). Touches only `infra/scripts/` + `tests/` — no overlap with epic eb64 (`_cli/`, `.github/workflows/`, `_commands/`). Rebased clean onto latest origin/main.\n\nCommit `59d1487` · Change-Id `Ie52bb8f671d3b89bdc0fec5b1943ed30caab95b0` · `rebar-ticket: 1890-7d05-eabc-4ac1` trailer resolves · DCO signed. Pushing to `gerrit HEAD:refs/for/main`; will land only on LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1, then close."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788069271823303580,"uuid":"a79b8c29-910d-4e16-a7d5-0e6dccc9182a"}